m:main","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9e6a0437420e88fdf83667384fe2ebe31028f69b51c985b51bc199dd41e020fa","file":"preprints/The-Boltzmann-Grad-limit-for-stable-radial-potentials-on-regular-kinetic-intervals-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":46,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"03a17e8b7fd2331d58775e652366eba4780139e2fa5a8189ec42378cd14b6443","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Boltzmann-Grad-limit-for-stable-radial-potentials-on-regular-kinetic-intervals-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9e6a0437420e88fdf83667384fe2ebe31028f69b51c985b51bc199dd41e020fa","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Boltzmann-Grad-limit-for-stable-radial-potentials-on-regular-kinetic-intervals-September-23-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L46"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $\\Phi$ satisfy Assumption~\\ref{pre:potential}, and let $\\beta>0$.\nLet $f_0\\ge0$ be a $C^1$ probability density on $\\R^3\\times\\R^3$ such that\n\\begin{equation}\\label{intro:data-bound}\n \\|f_0\\|_{\\mathrm{Bol},2\\beta}\n +\\|\\nabla_xf_0\\|_{\\mathrm{Bol},2\\beta}<\\infty.\n\\end{equation}\nFix $0<T<\\infty$ for which the equation\n\\begin{equation}\\label{intro:boltzmann}\n (\\partial_t+v\\cdot\\nabla_x)f=Q_\\Phi(f,f),\n \\qquad f|_{t=0}=f_0,\n\\end{equation}\nhas a nonnegative classical probability-density solution satisfying\n\\begin{equation}\\label{intro:solution-bound}\n \\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\\sup_{x,v}\n e^{2\\beta|v|^2}f(t,x,v)<\\infty.\n\\end{equation}\nStart the exact Newtonian process from the grand-canonical law\n\\eqref{pre:model}. For its scaled factorial densities\n$F_s^\\varepsilon$, defined in \\eqref{pre:factorial}, every fixed\ninteger $s\\ge1$ satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{intro:chaos}\n \\lim_{\\varepsilon\\downarrow0}\\;\n \\sup_{0\\le t\\le T}\n \\bigl\\|F_s^\\varepsilon(t)-f(t)^{\\otimes s}\\bigr\\|_\n {L^1((\\R^3\\times\\R^3)^s)}=0.\n\\end{equation}"}
